1
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:12,610
LEE JAE-IN, KIM WOO-SEOK, CHOI YE-BIN

2
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:16,850
CHA WOO-MIN, AN JI-HO, JUNG SO-RI

3
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:20,930
SCRIPTWRITER: KANG MIN-JI

4
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:25,010
DIRECTOR: IM DAE-WOONG

5
00:00:27,010 --> 00:00:31,317
NIGHT HAS COME

6
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:33,010
ALL PEOPLE, ORGANIZATIONS, LOCATIONS,

7
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:34,650
AND INCIDENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS.

8
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:39,970
EPISODE 3

9
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:54,410
<i>Kim Dong-hyun was a Citizen.</i>

10
00:01:19,290 --> 00:01:21,650
Hey, they're back.

11
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:30,170
What happened to Dong-hyun?

12
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:34,970
Say something.

13
00:01:34,995 --> 00:01:36,195
What happened to Dong-hyun?

14
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,970
What's going on?

15
00:01:38,490 --> 00:01:39,570
He thought...

16
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:42,810
...the line stopped there.

17
00:01:45,210 --> 00:01:46,570
So he was checking.

18
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:49,370
Then he slipped.

19
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:55,450
Then how far into the
village were you able to go?

20
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:00,265
You said you would meet
people and call the police.

21
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:01,490
Did you do it?

22
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:04,690
We couldn't go.

23
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:07,615
The entire place is enclosed with the line.

24
00:02:13,650 --> 00:02:15,050
We're completely locked in here.

25
00:02:16,664 --> 00:02:19,424
Then does it mean...

26
00:02:20,490 --> 00:02:23,210
...we can't leave this
place until the game is over?

27
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:26,290
Yes.

28
00:02:56,153 --> 00:02:56,970
Are you crying?

29
00:03:01,663 --> 00:03:02,743
If...

30
00:03:03,688 --> 00:03:05,408
...I didn't say...

31
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:08,530
...we could try going to the mountain,

32
00:03:11,143 --> 00:03:12,703
he wouldn't have died.

33
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,570
That was a stupid thing to say.

34
00:03:21,841 --> 00:03:25,161
It's all my fault that Dong-hyun is dead.

35
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:31,800
You didn't make him go.

36
00:03:32,431 --> 00:03:33,911
They volunteered to go.

37
00:03:35,367 --> 00:03:37,170
You didn't know there
wouldn't be a way out.

38
00:03:38,970 --> 00:03:40,804
You can't blame yourself
for not knowing that.

39
00:03:45,014 --> 00:03:45,890
So...

40
00:03:47,295 --> 00:03:48,375
...what will you do?

41
00:03:51,639 --> 00:03:53,639
We can't leave this place
until the game is over.

42
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:55,930
Are you just going to cry here?

43
00:03:58,447 --> 00:03:59,290
No.

44
00:04:02,657 --> 00:04:04,257
We must find another way out.

45
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:30,570
Hello?

46
00:04:34,985 --> 00:04:35,825
Hello?

47
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:37,490
Hey!

48
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:39,450
Come on.

49
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:06,850
Where are you going?

50
00:05:10,487 --> 00:05:11,330
Oh, hey.

51
00:05:13,050 --> 00:05:14,890
Kyung-jun and the other
guys wanted to see me.

52
00:05:16,001 --> 00:05:17,481
Don't go if you don't want to go.

53
00:05:18,570 --> 00:05:20,090
I should still go.

54
00:05:34,170 --> 00:05:35,050
Why?

55
00:05:39,064 --> 00:05:40,584
Why?

56
00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,890
Hey, Jun-hee!

57
00:05:45,810 --> 00:05:46,970
What are you doing?

58
00:05:48,650 --> 00:05:49,770
Isn't the phone ringing?

59
00:05:50,690 --> 00:05:51,690
What's wrong?

60
00:05:52,671 --> 00:05:53,711
Hello?

61
00:05:55,970 --> 00:05:56,970
Forget it.

62
00:05:57,825 --> 00:05:58,945
What's wrong?

63
00:06:01,530 --> 00:06:02,490
It's fake.

64
00:06:03,210 --> 00:06:05,090
-Everything is.
-What?

65
00:06:09,650 --> 00:06:11,490
The phones were never connected.

66
00:06:16,090 --> 00:06:17,090
What is this?

67
00:06:27,983 --> 00:06:29,463
RETREAT CENTER COMMITTEE

68
00:06:32,250 --> 00:06:33,690
ACCOUNTING AND FINANCES
OF MURYEONG RETREAT CENTER

69
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:40,410
Look at this.

70
00:06:41,405 --> 00:06:42,485
The files are empty.

71
00:06:54,361 --> 00:06:55,801
SWIMMING POOL CAFETERIA

72
00:06:56,690 --> 00:06:58,330
You love this sesame-seed-flavored ramyeon.

73
00:06:59,290 --> 00:07:00,130
Right.

74
00:07:00,210 --> 00:07:01,090
Thank you.

75
00:07:01,810 --> 00:07:03,970
The ramyeon preference is the
only thing we have in common.

76
00:07:04,810 --> 00:07:06,890
Then do you have a
different preference for music?

77
00:07:06,970 --> 00:07:07,850
Darn you.

78
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:08,930
Do you have a death wish?

79
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:10,810
Don't shove that perverted music on me.

80
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:12,570
Okay, chill.

81
00:07:12,650 --> 00:07:13,890
I won't do that.

82
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:21,290
Nerd.

83
00:07:22,239 --> 00:07:23,599
You're the game expert.

84
00:07:24,517 --> 00:07:25,797
Is this an existing game?

85
00:07:28,441 --> 00:07:29,250
No.

86
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:30,570
It's my first time seeing it too.

87
00:07:33,810 --> 00:07:35,690
But I'm not a nerd.

88
00:07:37,609 --> 00:07:38,849
Okay, sorry.

89
00:07:39,185 --> 00:07:41,705
So what should we do to win this game?

90
00:07:41,730 --> 00:07:44,090
It's the same as playing the Mafia Game.

91
00:07:46,210 --> 00:07:47,570
Haven't you played it before?

92
00:07:48,423 --> 00:07:50,263
You don't think I know that, you punk?

93
00:07:53,490 --> 00:07:55,490
Everyone's identities are not revealed...

94
00:07:55,970 --> 00:07:58,090
...until they die.

95
00:07:58,490 --> 00:08:01,250
You have to find out
who your opponents are.

96
00:08:01,937 --> 00:08:04,457
The Doctors and Police
are on the Citizens' side.

97
00:08:05,250 --> 00:08:07,850
The team that wipes out
the other team will win.

98
00:08:08,770 --> 00:08:11,970
Darn it.

99
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:13,730
It'll take forever to find the Mafia.

100
00:08:15,814 --> 00:08:16,470
Hey.

101
00:08:17,927 --> 00:08:19,626
Why don't we just kill off random people?

102
00:08:20,496 --> 00:08:21,930
Then the game will end.

103
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:24,130
You said you were a Citizen too.

104
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:25,385
We can just get rid of the Mafia.

105
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:26,490
Why kill off other people?

106
00:08:26,593 --> 00:08:28,993
It said we had to wipe out
the other team, you idiot.

107
00:08:29,704 --> 00:08:31,824
Why do you want to kill
off people on your team too?

108
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:33,345
You can't even follow through with it.

109
00:08:33,370 --> 00:08:34,250
Stop acting tough.

110
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:37,090
You were super scared
when you saw the kids dying.

111
00:08:37,170 --> 00:08:40,050
-I was never scared, you jerk!
-Shut your mouth!

112
00:08:45,370 --> 00:08:46,410
Choi Ju-won.

113
00:08:49,121 --> 00:08:50,641
Why did he die when he was Mafia?

114
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:54,410
I don't know why he died either.

115
00:08:59,450 --> 00:09:02,890
The rule said the Mafia
had to execute someone.

116
00:09:03,970 --> 00:09:06,530
I don't know what happened,
but maybe, the Mafia had...

117
00:09:06,555 --> 00:09:08,355
...a good reason to kill
Ju-won instead of a Citizen.

118
00:09:09,890 --> 00:09:11,650
What if a Citizen were to kill the Mafia?

119
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:14,290
Is that allowed?

120
00:09:15,290 --> 00:09:17,650
That wasn't in the rules, so I'm not sure.

121
00:09:21,210 --> 00:09:22,330
Instead of playing this game,

122
00:09:23,530 --> 00:09:25,610
let's find all the Mafia and
gather them in one place.

123
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:27,570
Then we should make them kill each other.

124
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:31,050
-That's a great idea.
-Right?

125
00:09:31,130 --> 00:09:32,250
That's an awesome idea.

126
00:09:32,330 --> 00:09:33,650
-Right?
-Totally.

127
00:09:33,770 --> 00:09:36,490
Gosh, you idiots.

128
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:38,290
Your idea is awful.

129
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:40,250
Do you think that would work?

130
00:09:48,290 --> 00:09:51,890
What if one of us dies
again tonight like Ju-won?

131
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:59,330
We should hide and lock the door.

132
00:10:00,970 --> 00:10:03,370
Are you going to vote?

133
00:10:05,170 --> 00:10:06,250
We have to.

134
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:09,410
But how many people are in the Mafia?

135
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,760
I don't know.

136
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:13,490
It doesn't say anything about their number.

137
00:10:15,068 --> 00:10:15,890
Right.

138
00:10:16,332 --> 00:10:17,193
The Police.

139
00:10:17,625 --> 00:10:19,545
There was an announcement that the
Police used their skill this morning.

140
00:10:19,570 --> 00:10:20,970
They must know then.

141
00:10:21,850 --> 00:10:23,370
Are you really all Citizens?

142
00:10:24,216 --> 00:10:25,656
None of us are Police?

143
00:10:26,970 --> 00:10:27,730
Darn it.

144
00:10:29,690 --> 00:10:31,330
-Look at this.
-Hey.

145
00:10:31,410 --> 00:10:32,650
Be quiet!

146
00:10:32,909 --> 00:10:34,109
You're distracting me.

147
00:10:35,711 --> 00:10:37,690
If you plan to vote,
let's call Jun-hee here.

148
00:10:38,456 --> 00:10:39,450
Get Jun-hee.

149
00:10:43,610 --> 00:10:45,730
Can't she get him herself?

150
00:10:46,192 --> 00:10:47,272
Darn it.

151
00:10:48,632 --> 00:10:49,632
What about Na-hee?

152
00:10:51,265 --> 00:10:52,105
I don't know.

153
00:10:52,130 --> 00:10:53,575
She's probably sleeping in the infirmary.

154
00:10:55,481 --> 00:10:56,890
Park Woo-ram!

155
00:10:57,237 --> 00:10:58,237
Get Na-hee too.

156
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,040
When I got injured,

157
00:11:10,817 --> 00:11:12,730
I should have said I was in pain
and stopped us from going.

158
00:11:15,056 --> 00:11:17,919
If we had come right back,
that wouldn't have happened.

159
00:11:21,669 --> 00:11:22,530
No.

160
00:11:24,535 --> 00:11:26,255
Even if you said you wanted to go back,

161
00:11:27,527 --> 00:11:29,327
they could have kept going anyway.

162
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:32,360
It's not your fault.

163
00:11:34,048 --> 00:11:34,890
But still.

164
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,400
Everyone is responsible.

165
00:11:40,598 --> 00:11:42,970
I saw Dong-hyun die right in front of me.

166
00:11:44,751 --> 00:11:46,191
But I couldn't do anything.

167
00:11:54,736 --> 00:11:55,610
Hyun-ho.

168
00:11:57,638 --> 00:11:59,398
Let's stay alive and get out of this place.

169
00:12:00,718 --> 00:12:04,478
I'll protect you, no matter what.

170
00:12:06,423 --> 00:12:07,423
You will?

171
00:12:08,158 --> 00:12:09,438
When we get out of here,

172
00:12:10,465 --> 00:12:12,345
I want to watch you play.

173
00:12:21,518 --> 00:12:22,918
Don't fall for me when you do.

174
00:12:45,518 --> 00:12:47,558
You know, the person who
created this Mafia Game...

175
00:12:50,238 --> 00:12:52,398
What's the reason behind
putting us through this?

176
00:12:54,564 --> 00:12:56,084
We must find out who made this game...

177
00:12:56,118 --> 00:12:57,318
...and the reason behind it.

178
00:12:58,998 --> 00:13:00,998
Where do you think the
creator of this game is?

179
00:13:02,678 --> 00:13:04,398
It's just us here.

180
00:13:07,198 --> 00:13:09,238
Maybe, the creator comes
in when we fall asleep.

181
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:12,965
Maybe, that's when
the creator killed Ju-won.

182
00:13:12,990 --> 00:13:15,190
It said the Mafia killed Ju-won.

183
00:13:16,509 --> 00:13:19,232
But only the students from our class
are on the list of participants.

184
00:13:20,798 --> 00:13:23,370
If there was someone else,
the name would've been on the list.

185
00:13:24,158 --> 00:13:25,050
Right.

186
00:13:25,958 --> 00:13:27,518
The creator probably selected the Mafia...

187
00:13:27,543 --> 00:13:29,010
...when assigning the identities.

188
00:13:31,758 --> 00:13:32,758
Then...

189
00:13:35,918 --> 00:13:39,238
...someone in our class
really killed Ju-won?

190
00:13:40,398 --> 00:13:41,678
According to the rules,

191
00:13:43,318 --> 00:13:44,398
probably.

192
00:13:54,638 --> 00:13:57,798
Then who do you think might be the Mafia?

193
00:13:58,878 --> 00:14:00,598
Seeing how Ju-won died,

194
00:14:00,998 --> 00:14:02,610
it might be someone from Kyung-jun's gang.

195
00:14:02,998 --> 00:14:03,610
Right.

196
00:14:04,088 --> 00:14:06,248
They bullied Ju-won a lot.

197
00:14:06,447 --> 00:14:07,887
It looked like Jin-ha and
Seung-bin borrowed...

198
00:14:07,935 --> 00:14:09,770
...a lot of money from Ju-won too.

199
00:14:11,158 --> 00:14:13,158
I'm not sure about Ju-won.

200
00:14:14,678 --> 00:14:17,398
Usually, the Mafia would
want to kill off Citizens.

201
00:14:19,758 --> 00:14:20,798
We might be able to learn something...

202
00:14:20,823 --> 00:14:22,023
...from yesterday's vote.

203
00:14:23,198 --> 00:14:25,958
Let's kill Heo Yul.

204
00:14:32,798 --> 00:14:34,638
Why are you looking at me?

205
00:14:35,758 --> 00:14:36,758
Well,

206
00:14:37,118 --> 00:14:39,598
you wanted everyone to
vote for Heo Yul yesterday.

207
00:14:40,678 --> 00:14:42,398
I voted for him because you told me so.

208
00:14:42,478 --> 00:14:43,758
Choi Mi-na.

209
00:14:44,638 --> 00:14:46,078
You think I'm part of the Mafia?

210
00:14:46,478 --> 00:14:47,330
Eun-ha.

211
00:14:48,478 --> 00:14:51,398
Why did you tell us he was Mafia?

212
00:14:57,398 --> 00:14:58,518
I'm not part of the Mafia.

213
00:14:58,878 --> 00:15:00,998
Do you think I killed Yul on purpose?

214
00:15:01,078 --> 00:15:01,958
You took the lead in that round,

215
00:15:01,983 --> 00:15:03,303
and that's how Yul ended up dead.

216
00:15:04,238 --> 00:15:05,238
Right?

217
00:15:05,638 --> 00:15:07,318
That's true.

218
00:15:09,758 --> 00:15:11,678
What are you guys doing?

219
00:15:17,158 --> 00:15:18,238
Hey, Kim So-mi.

220
00:15:19,078 --> 00:15:20,398
Then why did you do it?

221
00:15:20,958 --> 00:15:21,730
Me?

222
00:15:23,158 --> 00:15:23,890
Do what?

223
00:15:25,158 --> 00:15:27,198
I saw you push Dong-hyun at the mountain.

224
00:15:27,478 --> 00:15:29,078
Hey, I'm slipping down.

225
00:15:35,718 --> 00:15:37,438
He died because of you!

226
00:15:37,678 --> 00:15:38,678
Have you gone mad?

227
00:15:39,622 --> 00:15:40,982
You think I pushed him?

228
00:15:48,678 --> 00:15:49,998
No, that's not true.

229
00:15:51,438 --> 00:15:54,998
I almost died stopping
Kim Dong-hyun from falling.

230
00:15:55,078 --> 00:15:56,173
The other guys saw it.

231
00:15:56,198 --> 00:15:57,318
What are you on about?

232
00:15:57,398 --> 00:15:59,278
Guys, I really had no idea all this.

233
00:15:59,303 --> 00:16:00,623
It was just a joke.

234
00:16:00,878 --> 00:16:03,078
But she pushed him on purpose
when she knew he was going to die.

235
00:16:03,103 --> 00:16:04,583
I never did.

236
00:16:05,238 --> 00:16:07,678
Tell Jun-hee and the other kids to come.

237
00:16:07,838 --> 00:16:09,398
Ask the other kids!

238
00:16:09,478 --> 00:16:11,878
-Hey!
-Stop it.

239
00:16:17,198 --> 00:16:18,238
There's nothing.

240
00:16:22,038 --> 00:16:23,318
Can I...

241
00:16:31,078 --> 00:16:32,478
Nice.

242
00:16:32,798 --> 00:16:33,798
What are you doing?

243
00:16:34,271 --> 00:16:36,645
I need to check whether
you're on my side or not...

244
00:16:36,678 --> 00:16:37,998
...before having a meal with you.

245
00:16:38,798 --> 00:16:39,638
What are you talking about?

246
00:16:39,663 --> 00:16:40,543
Give me my phone back.

247
00:16:45,038 --> 00:16:47,358
Hey, is it any good?

248
00:16:51,158 --> 00:16:52,478
Darn it!

249
00:16:52,798 --> 00:16:54,798
Stay still!

250
00:16:55,038 --> 00:16:56,718
If I spill any, you're dead.

251
00:16:56,743 --> 00:16:58,223
It's one punch for each drop.

252
00:17:02,198 --> 00:17:03,198
VOTE

253
00:17:03,278 --> 00:17:04,798
Darn it.

254
00:17:05,438 --> 00:17:06,413
It's the same as ours.

255
00:17:06,438 --> 00:17:07,398
It won't show his occupation.

256
00:17:07,478 --> 00:17:08,558
Darn it.

257
00:17:11,878 --> 00:17:14,358
Gosh, I spilled it.

258
00:17:22,078 --> 00:17:23,398
Give me my phone back now.

259
00:17:23,718 --> 00:17:24,598
Wait.

260
00:17:24,623 --> 00:17:25,743
I'm not done checking yet.

261
00:17:26,638 --> 00:17:27,718
Check what?

262
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:31,958
If I can vote with someone else's phone,

263
00:17:32,238 --> 00:17:34,398
it means I can give all the
votes to the person I want.

264
00:17:39,118 --> 00:17:40,278
Kneel.

265
00:17:41,745 --> 00:17:42,825
Get off me!

266
00:17:43,398 --> 00:17:44,398
Let me go!

267
00:17:45,998 --> 00:17:46,998
Hey.

268
00:17:48,078 --> 00:17:49,038
Pick one.

269
00:17:49,118 --> 00:17:50,078
I'll vote for that person.

270
00:17:50,838 --> 00:17:51,878
No.

271
00:17:54,558 --> 00:17:55,558
Then it'll be you.

272
00:17:55,718 --> 00:17:56,718
Don't do that.

273
00:17:56,798 --> 00:17:58,478
No!

274
00:17:58,558 --> 00:18:01,598
Stop it!

275
00:18:01,758 --> 00:18:03,078
I said no!

276
00:18:03,158 --> 00:18:04,638
Stop!

277
00:18:05,558 --> 00:18:06,638
<i>Failed to vote</i>

278
00:18:06,758 --> 00:18:09,518
I guess you can't vote
on someone else's phone.

279
00:18:09,758 --> 00:18:10,650
Gosh.

280
00:18:22,198 --> 00:18:23,038
Hey.

281
00:18:23,118 --> 00:18:23,998
I was looking for you.

282
00:18:24,023 --> 00:18:25,823
Everyone's saying they're going to vote.

283
00:18:26,296 --> 00:18:28,410
Yul died after we voted,
and they want to vote again?

284
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:30,958
We can't leave until the game is over.

285
00:18:32,078 --> 00:18:33,118
We have no choice.

286
00:18:33,198 --> 00:18:35,078
Still, how can we do that again?

287
00:18:36,438 --> 00:18:37,638
We have to stop them.

288
00:18:38,558 --> 00:18:40,038
We must not vote.

289
00:18:40,278 --> 00:18:41,438
How are we going to stop them?

290
00:18:42,118 --> 00:18:43,133
Even if we want to persuade them,

291
00:18:43,158 --> 00:18:44,198
we need an alternative.

292
00:18:45,075 --> 00:18:46,374
I'll persuade them.

293
00:18:46,571 --> 00:18:47,931
Is everyone together?

294
00:18:48,078 --> 00:18:49,918
No, in their rooms.

295
00:18:50,638 --> 00:18:51,958
Then let's gather them first.

296
00:18:52,438 --> 00:18:53,410
I'll help.

297
00:18:53,718 --> 00:18:54,918
Wait, Da-beom.

298
00:18:55,518 --> 00:18:57,358
He left when Go Kyung-jun called him.

299
00:18:57,646 --> 00:18:59,646
Those punks.

300
00:19:00,718 --> 00:19:02,278
I never liked them.

301
00:19:03,798 --> 00:19:04,998
Let me go!

302
00:19:05,078 --> 00:19:06,478
Just wait.

303
00:19:14,478 --> 00:19:15,478
Stay still.

304
00:19:19,878 --> 00:19:21,598
It won't work.

305
00:19:24,638 --> 00:19:25,758
This is messed up.

306
00:19:27,798 --> 00:19:28,798
Hey!

307
00:19:30,758 --> 00:19:31,798
That's enough.

308
00:19:34,758 --> 00:19:35,838
What on earth are you doing?

309
00:19:35,918 --> 00:19:37,078
What's your deal?

310
00:19:37,638 --> 00:19:38,878
-You scared me.
-Get up.

311
00:19:38,958 --> 00:19:40,398
Get up, Da-beom.

312
00:19:41,158 --> 00:19:42,358
Three on one guy?

313
00:19:43,398 --> 00:19:44,798
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

314
00:19:46,038 --> 00:19:47,238
Where do you think you're going?

315
00:19:47,878 --> 00:19:49,038
Hey.

316
00:19:50,318 --> 00:19:51,438
Stop it.

317
00:19:52,118 --> 00:19:53,198
Come with me.

318
00:19:53,278 --> 00:19:54,158
I have something to say.

319
00:19:54,238 --> 00:19:55,838
Why do I have to listen to you?

320
00:19:55,918 --> 00:19:58,278
-Hey!
-Come on.

321
00:20:06,438 --> 00:20:07,638
You jerk.

322
00:20:08,377 --> 00:20:11,097
Why must I listen to you, you jerk?

323
00:20:13,838 --> 00:20:14,998
These jerks.

324
00:20:18,078 --> 00:20:19,758
You never get it when I say it nicely.

325
00:20:20,038 --> 00:20:21,558
I need to teach you a lesson.

326
00:20:31,878 --> 00:20:33,318
You jerk.

327
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:40,910
Take this!

328
00:20:45,518 --> 00:20:46,558
Come here.

329
00:20:57,998 --> 00:20:59,438
Let go of me.

330
00:20:59,463 --> 00:21:00,823
I said let go, you prick.

331
00:21:00,983 --> 00:21:02,023
Are you going to listen?

332
00:21:02,878 --> 00:21:04,598
Are you going to do as I say?

333
00:21:07,678 --> 00:21:09,598
I get it, jerk!

334
00:21:23,358 --> 00:21:24,358
Let's go.

335
00:21:30,398 --> 00:21:31,518
Hey!

336
00:21:32,438 --> 00:21:33,918
Come here.

337
00:21:36,038 --> 00:21:37,078
Hey.

338
00:21:37,558 --> 00:21:40,078
Will you stop for goodness' sake?

339
00:21:43,735 --> 00:21:45,895
Can I tell other kids what you just did?

340
00:21:47,758 --> 00:21:49,798
What do you think they'd say?

341
00:21:50,110 --> 00:21:51,710
Come to your senses.

342
00:21:53,038 --> 00:21:54,478
What's the point of talking to him?

343
00:21:56,638 --> 00:21:57,718
If we vote on you now,

344
00:21:57,743 --> 00:21:59,783
everyone else will vote after us.

345
00:22:01,038 --> 00:22:02,078
What do you say?

346
00:22:04,078 --> 00:22:05,118
Do you want me to press your name?

347
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:06,438
You wench.

348
00:22:07,438 --> 00:22:08,638
Drop it right now.

349
00:22:08,998 --> 00:22:11,598
I won't tell other kids,
so drop it right now.

350
00:22:15,438 --> 00:22:16,878
Please stop.

351
00:22:26,526 --> 00:22:28,278
Gosh.

352
00:22:32,669 --> 00:22:34,530
We're all going to gather
in the assembly hall.

353
00:22:35,998 --> 00:22:37,078
You should come too.

354
00:22:43,158 --> 00:22:44,398
Leave the cafeteria door open...

355
00:22:46,118 --> 00:22:47,158
...for the others to use.

356
00:22:59,238 --> 00:23:00,358
Darn it.

357
00:23:11,044 --> 00:23:13,965
PARTICIPANT LIST

358
00:23:15,135 --> 00:23:16,415
I gathered all of you here...

359
00:23:18,038 --> 00:23:20,038
...not to decide whom we should vote for,

360
00:23:20,862 --> 00:23:22,702
but to give up on voting.

361
00:23:23,838 --> 00:23:24,998
Give up on voting?

362
00:23:26,078 --> 00:23:27,158
Are you sure about that?

363
00:23:27,998 --> 00:23:29,718
If we vote, one person
is guaranteed to die.

364
00:23:30,798 --> 00:23:32,438
But if we don't, we'll all survive.

365
00:23:32,678 --> 00:23:35,238
What if we agreed not to vote,
but someone votes in secret?

366
00:23:35,598 --> 00:23:36,798
What are you going to do then?

367
00:23:37,038 --> 00:23:38,318
She has a point.

368
00:23:38,343 --> 00:23:39,403
How am I supposed to trust everyone?

369
00:23:41,158 --> 00:23:42,850
We should make everyone trust each other.

370
00:23:43,006 --> 00:23:45,846
We can collect all our phones,
so no one can vote.

371
00:23:48,878 --> 00:23:49,758
He's right.

372
00:23:49,783 --> 00:23:51,703
If we collect our phones, no one can vote.

373
00:23:52,198 --> 00:23:53,358
That'll work.

374
00:23:53,518 --> 00:23:55,078
Who's going to keep the phones?

375
00:23:55,398 --> 00:23:57,398
The person in charge
might change his or her mind.

376
00:23:57,678 --> 00:23:59,678
Let's keep them in the
center for everyone to see.

377
00:24:00,558 --> 00:24:02,878
Yes, we can all watch together.

378
00:24:03,238 --> 00:24:04,918
What if someone steals it?

379
00:24:07,318 --> 00:24:08,398
I'm not doing it.

380
00:24:08,478 --> 00:24:09,692
I'm not handing in my phone.

381
00:24:11,038 --> 00:24:12,438
I think it's a good idea.

382
00:24:12,518 --> 00:24:13,558
Let's hand in our phones.

383
00:24:14,638 --> 00:24:15,558
Are you crazy?

384
00:24:15,638 --> 00:24:16,798
Who'd steal your phone?

385
00:24:16,878 --> 00:24:17,878
Just hand it in.

386
00:24:17,958 --> 00:24:20,838
-No.
-Can't you live without your phone?

387
00:24:20,918 --> 00:24:22,678
-Don't.
-Why not?

388
00:24:22,758 --> 00:24:25,278
Why are you yelling at me?

389
00:24:25,303 --> 00:24:26,543
If we hand it in, no one will die.

390
00:24:26,607 --> 00:24:28,807
Oh, be quiet.

391
00:24:31,038 --> 00:24:33,518
The class president is
actually making sense for once.

392
00:24:34,318 --> 00:24:35,718
Why won't you cooperate?

393
00:24:39,496 --> 00:24:41,496
Hand in your phones, so no one can vote.

394
00:24:43,543 --> 00:24:45,250
Everyone, make sure to hand in your phones.

395
00:24:47,958 --> 00:24:49,318
Listen to me when I'm being nice.

396
00:24:59,798 --> 00:25:00,918
Hurry up.

397
00:25:01,958 --> 00:25:03,318
Hurry up and hand it in.

398
00:25:03,478 --> 00:25:05,238
Let's hurry since we have no time.

399
00:25:39,558 --> 00:25:41,998
<i>A minute left to vote.</i>

400
00:25:44,838 --> 00:25:46,358
Gosh.

401
00:25:52,678 --> 00:25:54,918
Darn it!

402
00:25:55,078 --> 00:25:56,598
Hey, Class President!

403
00:25:56,623 --> 00:25:58,023
Are you sure we're okay?

404
00:25:58,464 --> 00:25:59,864
Let's just wait.

405
00:26:00,198 --> 00:26:01,598
It's not midnight yet.

406
00:26:02,998 --> 00:26:03,890
Gosh.

407
00:26:20,038 --> 00:26:22,478
Hey.

408
00:26:22,878 --> 00:26:24,890
It's past midnight,
but there was no announcement.

409
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:26,798
Did it work?

410
00:26:29,358 --> 00:26:30,678
Are we okay now?

411
00:26:31,558 --> 00:26:33,078
We did it.

412
00:26:33,398 --> 00:26:36,078
-We're safe.
-It's over.

413
00:26:36,398 --> 00:26:37,438
We're safe.

414
00:26:46,398 --> 00:26:47,958
Are we okay now?

415
00:27:02,365 --> 00:27:06,405
<i>Participants must vote</i>
<i>and identify the Mafia.</i>

416
00:27:13,645 --> 00:27:16,525
PARTICIPANTS MUST VOTE
AND IDENTIFY THE MAFIA.

417
00:27:18,518 --> 00:27:19,364
Hey!

418
00:27:19,897 --> 00:27:20,964
What are you doing?

419
00:27:21,358 --> 00:27:22,438
What else?

420
00:27:23,063 --> 00:27:24,303
What if we do nothing and die?

421
00:27:24,863 --> 00:27:26,650
Are you going to take responsibility?

422
00:27:27,638 --> 00:27:28,678
She's right.

423
00:27:28,958 --> 00:27:30,278
Wait.

424
00:27:31,278 --> 00:27:32,718
We don't know yet.

425
00:27:33,078 --> 00:27:34,158
Don't know what?

426
00:27:34,998 --> 00:27:36,958
The game didn't end.

427
00:27:37,878 --> 00:27:39,318
What if we die listening to you?

428
00:27:39,878 --> 00:27:41,198
Are you going to be responsible?

429
00:27:42,278 --> 00:27:43,358
Hey!

430
00:27:44,838 --> 00:27:46,878
Stop blaming Jun-hee and calm down.

431
00:28:02,238 --> 00:28:05,598
<i>For breaking the rules, Lee Soo-bin...</i>

432
00:28:05,678 --> 00:28:08,558
<i>...and Park Ji-hoon will be executed.</i>

433
00:28:26,478 --> 00:28:32,038
<i>Lee Soo-bin and Park Ji-hoon were Citizens.</i>

434
00:28:33,358 --> 00:28:34,478
Did everyone hand it in?

435
00:28:38,678 --> 00:28:42,718
<i>Participants must vote</i>
<i>and identify the Mafia.</i>

436
00:28:42,798 --> 00:28:44,198
What do you think you're doing?

437
00:28:44,598 --> 00:28:46,798
Get your phone if you don't want to die.

438
00:28:48,758 --> 00:28:50,398
-Shoot.
-No.

439
00:28:50,478 --> 00:28:52,558
If we don't vote, we die!

440
00:28:53,238 --> 00:28:56,038
I have to vote!

441
00:28:57,158 --> 00:28:58,438
<i>For breaking the rules,</i>

442
00:28:58,518 --> 00:29:01,758
<i>Oh Jin-seok will be executed.</i>

443
00:29:01,838 --> 00:29:03,478
-No!
-We'll die!

444
00:29:05,878 --> 00:29:08,798
-No!
-Wait!

445
00:29:10,638 --> 00:29:13,038
-Wait.
-Where's my phone?

446
00:29:14,638 --> 00:29:16,278
Jun-hee, hurry up.

447
00:29:19,598 --> 00:29:20,598
Jun-hee.

448
00:29:23,078 --> 00:29:24,078
What are you doing?

449
00:29:25,518 --> 00:29:27,078
We're all going to die!

450
00:29:28,398 --> 00:29:29,318
Kim Jun-hee!

451
00:29:31,438 --> 00:29:33,078
ELECTRICAL SHOCK HAZARD

452
00:29:50,198 --> 00:29:52,398
Move!

453
00:29:52,478 --> 00:29:53,758
Get off me!

454
00:29:54,878 --> 00:29:58,878
<i>Oh Jin-seok was a Citizen.</i>

455
00:30:02,838 --> 00:30:05,558
-It's mine!
-No.

456
00:30:08,358 --> 00:30:10,918
Where is it?

457
00:30:10,998 --> 00:30:13,878
I found it!

458
00:30:19,078 --> 00:30:20,278
Idiots.

459
00:30:23,011 --> 00:30:27,986
NIGHT HAS COME

